# A member's verdict (core/modules/qualification/README.md "A member's verdict", "Routes"): set or
# clear the verdict of one criterion of a lead's current snapshot; the lead is decided again from the
# verdicts that count, with no model call. A member's session and contacts' reviews.write. `personId`
# is a person of your workspace with a scored lead: put it in http-client.private.env.json with your
# workspaceId. A write sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too (the api's origin
# check). Each answers the snapshot as GET …/snapshot does; 400 validation_failed for a criterion or a
# verdict off the lists, or a note past 500 characters; 404 score_snapshot_not_found for a lead never
# scored, lead_not_found for a person without a lead.

### PUT /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/qualification/leads/{personId}/verdicts/{criterion}: a member's verdict on the criterion, with an optional note; it counts instead of the model's
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/qualification/leads/{{personId}}/verdicts/location
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{ "verdict": "met", "note": "Works from the Berlin office." }

### DELETE /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/qualification/leads/{personId}/verdicts/{criterion}: clears the member's verdict; the model's counts again
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/qualification/leads/{{personId}}/verdicts/location
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
